# Copilot Instructions for HPC Scripts

When generating SLURM scripts or HPC job submissions:

1. Always reference cluster_specs.md for node specifications
2. Partition guidelines:
   - Use #SBATCH --partition=compute for general CPU jobs
   - Use #SBATCH --partition=gpu for GPU jobs (H100 or V100)
   - Use #SBATCH --partition=highmem for high-memory jobs
   - Use #SBATCH --partition=fat for very high-memory and compute intense jobs
3. Always include:
   - #SBATCH --job-name=DESCRIPTIVE_NAME
   - #SBATCH --output=logs/%x_%j.out
   - #SBATCH --error=logs/%x_%j.err
   - #SBATCH --mem=<specify explicitly, do not rely on defaults>
   - #SBATCH --time=HH:MM:SS
4. GPU jobs: Document that exclusive node access is currently required
5. Reference examples in hpc/slurm_examples/ for templates